// MENUDEF - the mod's own menu. ZDoom wiki: https://zdoom.org/wiki/MENUDEF
//
// A MENUDEF lump does not replace GZDoom's menus; it adds to them. The two
// directives used here:
//
//   OptionMenu "<name>"       declares a new menu screen.
//   AddOptionMenu "<name>"    APPENDS items to a menu that already exists,
//                             leaving the rest of the engine's menu intact.
//                             (GZDoom's own option menus are declared
//                             `protected`, which forbids a mod from adding
//                             Command/SafeCommand items - arbitrary console
//                             commands - but allows Submenu, Option and
//                             StaticText. Verified in-engine 2026-10-13.)
//
// WHY THERE IS NO CVAR OF OUR OWN FOR THE LANGUAGE.
// GZDoom already ships the `language` CVar, and it is archived: the engine
// writes it to the player's gzdoom.ini and reads it back next launch. That
// is exactly the persistence the CEO asked for, in the place a player
// expects their settings to live, and it is the ONLY key this mod ever
// touches in their config. A mod-owned CVar would be a second source of
// truth and a second thing written to their file.
// See docs/engine/adr/004-language-switch-and-difficulty-ladder.md.

// The three values GZDoom's `language` CVar can hold in this mod.
// "default" is GZDoom's code for the LANGUAGE section marked `default`
// (ours is `[enu default]`); "ru" selects `[ru]`; "auto" is the engine's
// own "ask the operating system", and it is the value in every config that
// has never been touched.
//
// WHY "auto" IS IN THE LIST (it was not, until 2026-10-13 - bug E3).
// An OptionString row whose CVar holds a value absent from its list has
// nothing to show and GZDoom draws "Unknown"
// (gzdoom.pk3:zscript/engine/ui/menu/optionmenuitems.zs). The mod used to
// hide that by having a ZScript OptionMenu subclass overwrite "auto" with
// the code auto had already resolved to. That subclass is gone and this
// row is the reason why:
//
//   GZDoom allows ZScript to write a CVar ONLY while the engine is
//   handling menu INPUT. In 4.14.2 `DMenu::InMenu` is raised around
//   exactly three calls - OnUIEvent, OnInputEvent and MenuEvent
//   (src/common/menu/menu.cpp:276-327) - and around nothing else. Init,
//   Ticker and Drawer all run with InMenu == 0, and a CVar write from
//   there aborts the VM with "Attempt to change CVAR 'language' outside
//   of menu code". Verified in-engine 2026-10-13 from BOTH hooks.
//   Opening this screen the ordinary way happened to survive only because
//   the submenu is built inside the PARENT menu's MenuEvent; `openmenu
//   SD_OptionsMenu` from the console, or a key bound to it, killed the
//   game. See docs/engine/adr/004-language-switch-and-difficulty-ladder.md.
//
// Declaring the value costs one line and writes nothing, so there is no
// longer any code of ours that can abort. Choosing English or Russian
// still writes the CVar - but through the engine's own Option row, during
// input handling, where it is legal - and the engine archives it.
//
// The labels are localized like everything else, so the Russian build names
// the languages in Russian. They are NOT endonyms ("Русский" inside the
// English menu) because Freedoom's font cannot draw Cyrillic yet and the
// entry would read as blank - debt T9.
//
// `OptionString`, NOT `OptionValue`. GZDoom has two list directives and they
// differ by the CVar's TYPE: OptionValue parses its left column as a NUMBER,
// OptionString as a string. `language` is a string CVar, so the OptionValue
// form is a parse error. It is not a soft one either - verified in-engine on
// 2026-10-13, GZDoom 4.14.2 aborts during startup (exit 255, the log stops
// at "M_Init: Init menus.") and the mod never reaches the title screen. The
// whole game fails to launch over one keyword, so do not "simplify" this.

OptionString "SD_LanguageValues"
{
	"auto",    "$SD_LANGVAL_AUTO"
	"default", "$SD_LANGVAL_EN"
	"ru",      "$SD_LANGVAL_RU"
}

// --- The difficulty menu --------------------------------------------------
// BUG E4, found in-engine 2026-10-13: the fifth rung, "Hero of the Soviet
// Union, posthumously", ran off the right edge of the screen and read
// "HERO OF THE SOVIET UNION, POSTHU". The name is the CEO's and is not the
// thing to change (docs/product/DIFFICULTY-NAMES.md owns it); the font is.
//
// GZDoom's skill menu draws its items in the list menu's default font,
// which for Doom is BigFont - roughly 12 px a character on a 320-wide
// screen, so about 26 characters fit and the name is 38. `Font` is the one
// directive that fixes it without touching the words. SmallFont puts all
// five rungs on screen whole, in red with a gold highlight, which is also
// the mod's palette.
//
// The rest of the block is GZDoom 4.14.2's own IfGame(Doom) branch copied
// verbatim (gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt, ListMenu "SkillMenu"), for the same
// reason as the main menu above: a redeclared LISTMENU replaces the
// engine's descriptor, so leaving a line out deletes it. The skill ITEMS
// are not listed because the engine builds them from MAPINFO's `skill`
// blocks; this descriptor only says where and in what font. Re-diff on an
// engine upgrade - debt T14.
LISTMENU "SkillMenu"
{
	Font "SmallFont", "Red", "Gold"
	StaticPatch 96, 14, "M_NEWG", 0, "$MNU_NEWGAME"
	StaticPatch 54, 38, "M_SKILL", 0, "$MNU_CHOOSESKILL"
	LineSpacing 12
	Position 48, 63
}

// --- The main menu logo ---------------------------------------------------
// BUG E1 (found by the CEO on docs/qa/evidence/2026-10-13_0100_F2_title-and-menu.png):
// on the title screen the menu's M_DOOM block did not land on the name block
// painted into TITLEPIC, and a "CO" of the latter showed past its left edge.
//
// It was this lump's fault, not the art's. `art-director` generates both
// images from one lockup and records where the loose copy belongs:
// work/art/shell/manifest.json says M_DOOM goes at x=60, y=0 of the 320x200
// screen. Measured 2026-10-13: overlaying assets/graphics/shell/M_DOOM.png
// on TITLEPIC.png at (60,0) gives a mean per-channel difference of 6, and
// 22 or more at every neighbouring offset - so the art is exact and the
// manifest is right.
//
// GZDoom, however, was never told. Its own gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt declares
//     LISTMENU "MainMenu" { ... StaticPatch 94, 2, "M_DOOM" ... }
// and a mod that ships no MainMenu of its own inherits those numbers: the
// logo was drawn 34 px right and 2 px down of where it was drawn into
// TITLEPIC. The whole fix is the StaticPatch line below.
//
// WHY THE WHOLE MENU IS REPEATED FOR ONE NUMBER. There is no "move that
// item" directive: ADDLISTMENU only APPENDS, which here would draw a SECOND
// logo and leave the misplaced one in place. Redeclaring a LISTMENU replaces
// the engine's descriptor outright (verified in-engine 2026-10-13: five
// items, not ten), so every item has to be restated. The body below is
// GZDoom 4.14.2's own IfGame(Doom) branch copied verbatim, including the
// IfOption tests, so a player's "swap menu" and "show ReadThis" settings
// keep working. Re-diff it against gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt when the engine
// is upgraded.
//
// The item graphics (M_NGAME, M_OPTION...) are still Freedoom's red Doom
// lettering. Replacing them is art's call, not this lump's; debt T12.
LISTMENU "MainMenu"
{
	LineSpacing 16
	StaticPatch 60, 0, "M_DOOM"
	Position 97, 72
	IfOption(ReadThis)
	{
		Position 97, 64
	}

	PatchItem "M_NGAME", "n", "PlayerclassMenu"
	IfOption(SwapMenu)
	{
		PatchItem "M_LOADG", "l", "LoadGameMenu", 0
		PatchItem "M_SAVEG", "s", "SaveGameMenu", 0
		PatchItem "M_OPTION", "o", "OptionsMenu", 0
	}
	else
	{
		PatchItem "M_OPTION", "o", "OptionsMenu", 0
		PatchItem "M_LOADG", "l", "LoadGameMenu", 0
		PatchItem "M_SAVEG", "s", "SaveGameMenu", 0
	}
	IfOption(ReadThis)
	{
		PatchItem "M_RDTHIS", "r", "ReadThisMenu", 0
	}
	PatchItem "M_QUITG", "q", "QuitMenu", 0
}

OptionMenu "SD_OptionsMenu"
{
	Title "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE"
	Option "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGUAGE", "language", "SD_LanguageValues"
	StaticText " "
	StaticText "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGHELP"
	// Temporary while debt T9 (the Cyrillic font) is open. Delete this line
	// and its LANGUAGE ids in the same change that lands the glyphs.
	StaticText "$SD_OPTMNU_LANGWARN"
}

// --- Getting there --------------------------------------------------------
// BUG E2, found in-engine 2026-10-13: the mod's screen was attached to
// "OptionsMenu" alone, and the player could not reach it. GZDoom ships TWO
// options screens - the long one ("OptionsMenu", gzdoom.pk3/menudef.txt) and
// a short one for newcomers ("OptionsMenuSimple", gzdoom.pk3/menudef.zsimple)
// - and picks between them at the moment the item is activated:
//
//     case NAME_Optionsmenu:
//         if (m_simpleoptions) menu = NAME_OptionsmenuSimple;
//                       -- gzdoom 4.14.2, src/menu/doommenu.cpp:271
//
// `m_simpleoptions` is archived and defaults to TRUE, so on a fresh install
// "Options" opens the SHORT screen and our entry, appended to the long one,
// was nowhere. The player found it only after turning the simple menu off,
// or through "Full options menu". Both screens therefore get the entry.
//
// This is append, not replace: a protected menu rejects Command and
// SafeCommand from a mod but accepts Submenu, Option and StaticText.
//
// AddOptionMenu on a name the engine does not define is a hard parse error
// ("%s is not an option menu that can be extended", menudef.cpp:1249), so
// both names below are load-bearing: if a future GZDoom drops the simple
// menu, this lump stops loading until the line goes. Debt T13.
//
// `BEFORE "os_Menu"` puts the entry in the MIDDLE of the list instead of
// appending it. Appending looked right and was not: both screens already
// run to the bottom of a 200-line screen, and the new row landed under the
// last visible one - present, reachable by scrolling, and invisible to
// anyone who did not know to scroll (seen in-engine 2026-10-13).
// "os_Menu" is the Option Search entry, which both screens have; the
// engine matches on an item's ACTION, and when it finds no match it
// silently appends instead of failing (GetInsertIndex, menudef.cpp:802),
// so a renamed anchor degrades to the old behaviour rather than breaking.
AddOptionMenu "OptionsMenuSimple" BEFORE "os_Menu"
{
	Submenu "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE", "SD_OptionsMenu"
	StaticText " "
}

AddOptionMenu "OptionsMenu" BEFORE "os_Menu"
{
	Submenu "$SD_OPTMNU_TITLE", "SD_OptionsMenu"
	StaticText " "
}
